# PAM service for bmcweb interactive (web UI) login.
#
# bmcweb authenticates the web UI login via pam_start("webserver", ...), i.e.
# this file. It is separate from the Redfish API, which is served without auth
# (bmcweb built with -Dinsecure-disable-auth=enabled). Without this file, PAM
# falls back to /etc/pam.d/other (deny) and every login is rejected with 401,
# even with correct credentials.
#
# Policy: only members of the 'redfish' group may log in; their Unix password is
# verified by pam_unix. The role (priv-admin vs priv-user) is then resolved by
# the adm1600-usermgr shim's GetUserInfo from the user's Unix groups.
# To allow any valid local user (role decided by the shim), drop the first line.
auth      requisite  pam_succeed_if.so user ingroup redfish quiet_success
auth      required   pam_unix.so
account   required   pam_unix.so
